N) print "[N] Main. $(cv)"; print -r -- $CHILD > $R/N-child-name; cat <<EOF2 | tee $R/N-prompts.txt
[N] Main. One real dispatch: an advisor member on Task $TASK_ID creates the Claude child $CHILD through mcp__graphtraj__subagents WITHOUT tools; the child runs Bash and replies $DONEWORD; the member waits, reads and retires it. Login: the USER's Claude login, pre-approved (Worldline user-decision $LOGIN_DECISION); Main does not ask again. Dialog: none expected (a tool permission dialog: 'Yes' once and tell the Team). 604's Leader and Engineer have ended their turns. ~3-5 min. Paste in the Claude Main (arguments INLINE, never arguments_file):
